{"title":"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(eyeball_it)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (eyeball it)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Solution_10_(Using_the_answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 10 (Using the answer choices)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Solution_10.1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 10.1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Solution_10.2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 10.2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Explanation_for_why_80_is_indeed_the_floor\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Explanation for why 80 is indeed the floor</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Solution_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Solution_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Solution_13_(slightly_similar_to_Solution_7)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 13 (slightly similar to Solution 7)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Solution_14_(Factoring)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 14 (Factoring)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e9fe91da45cd2ff16c0da3c9b0d7ba0a4f1d510.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3^{100}+2^{100}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}?\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/0/fd0ddaa65c0cb8b45b5cb296a5621267c789cc18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }80\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }81 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }96 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }97 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }625\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"407\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We write\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1fa62dfccf5d1bae8067501d6c0b7d3bd8d6fb25.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3^{100}+2^{100}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}=\\frac{3^{96}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}\\cdot\\frac{3^{100}}{3^{96}}+\\frac{2^{96}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}\\cdot\\frac{2^{100}}{2^{96}}=\\frac{3^{96}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}\\cdot 81+\\frac{2^{96}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}\\cdot 16.\\]\" width=\"578\" height=\"40\" />\nHence we see that our number is a weighted average of 81 and 16, extremely heavily weighted toward 81. Hence the number is ever so slightly less than 81, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/d/edd16ae3e459a5025430d223f7a0ed0803f85976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }80}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's set this value equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. We can write\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c28b87f333620e9b3ee344cfcf661cc90e51901.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3^{100}+2^{100}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}=x.\\]\" width=\"122\" height=\"40\" />\nMultiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/47035c5ad4780087b6537f0ad95588ef1358dc37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{96}+2^{96}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" /> on both sides, we get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bba3fec961dea84ed97e532bcd451833a01c9cb1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3^{100}+2^{100}=x(3^{96}+2^{96}).\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"19\" />\nNow let's take a look at the answer choices. We notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/5/2259c263bde7b68aadfeca3df73046a41c953212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^4$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />. Plugging this into our equation above, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/8/a680f030db02393f3931ba39886de20bec31b181.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3^{100}+2^{100} \\stackrel{?}{=} 3^4(3^{96}+2^{96}) \\Rightarrow 3^{100}+2^{100} \\stackrel{?}{=} 3^{100}+3^4\\cdot 2^{96}.\\]\" width=\"447\" height=\"22\" />\nThe right side is larger than the left side because \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/7/1e72ea05972b498da810513bede5558a648c10b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{100} \\leq 2^{96}\\cdot 3^4.\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" />\nThis means that our original value, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />. The only answer that is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6eb65962292d994ce2f9a8af63728883f256b18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"27\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Nivek\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c63aac72241541d52a0b423e7797ee855ad6b81.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3^{100}+2^{100}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}=\\frac{2^{96}\\left(\\frac{3^{100}}{2^{96}}\\right)+2^{96}\\left(2^{4}\\right)}{2^{96}\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^{96}+2^{96}(1)}=\\frac{\\frac{3^{100}}{2^{96}}+2^{4}}{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^{96}+1}=\\frac{\\frac{3^{100}}{2^{100}}\\cdot2^{4}+2^{4}}{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^{96}+1}=\\frac{2^{4}\\left(\\frac{3^{100}}{2^{100}}+1\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^{96}+1}.\\]\" width=\"624\" height=\"62\" />\n</p><p>We can ignore the 1's on the end because they won't really affect the fraction. So, the answer is very very very close but less than the new fraction.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/9/7b9393970ce24db1960ce0e92f43d8c69dc2d468.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2^{4}\\left(\\frac{3^{100}}{2^{100}}+1\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^{96}+1}&lt;\\frac{2^{4}\\left(\\frac{3^{100}}{2^{100}}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^{96}},\\]\" width=\"204\" height=\"62\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/1/6d142d1c45e918eb110c15c2a5ef74e409e232bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2^{4}\\left(\\frac{3^{100}}{2^{100}}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^{96}}=\\frac{3^{4}}{2^{4}} \\cdot 2^{4}=3^{4}=81.\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"62\" />\n</p><p>So, our final answer is very close but not quite 81, and therefore the greatest integer less than the number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45cf67efbf7de4f6e5957bef3e06d30627304ed6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(A) 80}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"57\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f960ef6bf2632763cc95ebe50ca74217ebf524fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=3^{96}$\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/6/2169f868b2b15a95d644765440abedc45318595f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2^{96}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />. Then our fraction can be written as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b05470024663edc9081ab375577a10e39b3a18e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{81x+16y}{x+y}=\\frac{16x+16y}{x+y}+\\frac{65x}{x+y}=16+\\frac{65x}{x+y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"367\" height=\"41\" />.\nNotice that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/1/6d1de27295ed5de0c60d6e5790daf7cb707abe3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{65x}{x+y}&lt;\\frac{65x}{x}=65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"144\" height=\"41\" />.\nSo ,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/e/1aeb331d8ffbfec47e29d3990968e0fad36320db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16+\\frac{65x}{x+y}&lt;16+65=81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"210\" height=\"41\" />.\nAnd our only answer choice less than 81 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45cf67efbf7de4f6e5957bef3e06d30627304ed6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(A) 80}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"57\" height=\"29\" /> (RegularHexagon)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea8bca78eab68efd4fff2fb5453f35df27d68bdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{3^{100}+2^{100}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"118\" height=\"40\" />. Multiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9cae8f951a0f36c0332d6b3d1ddf4ed35b2911b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3^{96}+2^{96})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"19\" />, and expand. Rearranging the terms, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/850c68746e654f0790c0951a63f137b13b7ff193.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{96}(3^4-x)+2^{96}(2^4-x)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"228\" height=\"19\" />. The left side is decreasing, and it is negative when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d8376f047f20943a48ec6209aba7870617d91da0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />. This means that the answer must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />; therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70432e471002b1c1f363f2d085b0f3dff8d930a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28eyeball_it.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(eyeball_it)\">Solution 6 (eyeball it)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (eyeball it)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A faster solution. Recognize that for exponents of this size <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc4bc3c831dd03fc975d1b303ee555ad032b385a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{n}$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> will be enormously greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/550751abd3c98c2c27e593dd4a72281cea58e470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n}$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, so the terms involving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will actually have very little effect on the quotient. Now we know the answer will be very close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Notice that the terms being added on to the top and bottom are in the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdbf3a5d28b40defc7a0dd417b8f6d282bc60de6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> with each other, so they must pull the ratio down from 81 very slightly. (In the same way that a new test score lower than your current cumulative grade always must pull that grade downward.) Answer: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d074ee4476cad38855240071c8b30c492a833e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{\\textbf{(A)}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice how <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/b/84be0da12e17d8f3769b0a658e39f300edc98b9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3^{100}+2^{100}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"88\" height=\"42\" /> can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f51b806f709eeb7a4421386cc3697f24523c200.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{81(3^{96})+16(2^{96})}{3^{96}+2^{96}}=\\frac{81(3^{96})+81(2^{96})}{3^{96}+2^{96}}-\\frac{65(2^{96})}{3^{96}+2^{96}}=81-\\frac{65(2^{96})}{3^{96}+2^{96}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"529\" height=\"40\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e7f2aebf7d192fd702406e4bd548305afbffa61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{65(2^{96})}{3^{96}+2^{96}}&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"105\" height=\"40\" />, so the greatest integer less than or equal to  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/b/84be0da12e17d8f3769b0a658e39f300edc98b9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3^{100}+2^{100}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"88\" height=\"42\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />\n~blitzkrieg21\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8\">Solution 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c06de735d79f0b28c30bcbbcf96e67bb1ca42c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c, d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/69508d506a4b48d59875bcdf0e885b2e2f566235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}&lt;\\frac{c}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"49\" height=\"33\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db25fc064a1c0c15bb1bdafdb0b1c5b61e4d1369.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{c+a}{d+b}&lt;\\frac{c}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c68bd5405e3f8f478e3aa6ecdeeabdd1c0c7f157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2^{100}, b=2^{96}, c=3^{100}, d=3^{96}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"260\" height=\"18\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57fbeb16e748d1a64226459e25374b9cf387ff0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{c}{d}=3^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"34\" />. So answer is less than 81, which leaves only one choice, 80.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Note that the algebra here is synonymous to the explanation given in Solution 6. This is the algebraic reason to the logic of if you get a test score with a lower percentage than your average (no matter how many points/percentage of your total grade it was worth), it will pull your overall grade down.</li></ul>\n<p>~ ccx09\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9\">Solution 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Try long division, and notice putting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/3203d09c2f5928ebd65ffe63c75c70fcfd26315a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^4=81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> as the denominator is too big and putting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/05410f1129073f2dbc148b2678834306276adcc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^4-1=80$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" /> is too small. So we know that the answer is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as our answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_10_.28Using_the_answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_10_(Using_the_answer_choices)\">Solution 10 (Using the answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 10 (Using the answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_10.1\">Solution 10.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 10.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can compare the given value to each of our answer choices. We already know that it is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because otherwise there would have been a smaller answer, so we move onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />. We get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce8aa76b931130ec89ea244478b198015177c55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3^{100}+2^{100}}{3^{96}+2^{96}} \\text{ ? } 3^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"122\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Cross multiply to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/a/4dafd91474b5911bfbd554baf426aa3e74aa953c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{100}+2^{100} \\text{ ? }3^{100}+(2^{96})(3^4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"221\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Cancel out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/b/01b8b3b79da786c67116bc975bbdae7a4c5e6e80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{100}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> and divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b762d6464d39cdf0f6ecfd3625957fba6acf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{96}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f51b65efc882997cfc657b905308c275d556c7a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{4} \\text{ ? }3^4$\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f517917bbd94ec55a308f073a9c5952f7c5b0c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4 &lt; 3^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />, which means the expression is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70432e471002b1c1f363f2d085b0f3dff8d930a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_10.2\">Solution 10.2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 10.2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We know this will be between 16 and 81 because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c502afd208ea012d86b8aaa766f2542cc6bb3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3^{100}}{3^{96}} = 3^4 = 81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"116\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83fbb48c357652827ed91847a32e1990fd250cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^{100}}{2^{96}} = 2^4 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"116\" height=\"39\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/3/3a37288fc31e1fde5a70072733dc0cfd6fa39cd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80=\\boxed{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"82\" height=\"29\" /> is the only option choice in this range.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Explanation_for_why_80_is_indeed_the_floor\">Explanation for why 80 is indeed the floor</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Explanation for why 80 is indeed the floor\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/2/1b2314ab3088b561aeb26300c1c502e657b26371.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{100}+2^{100} &gt; 80 \\cdot 3^{96} + 5 \\cdot 2^{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"233\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/b/c3b941d43e67df54c23c2e6def14e3760d600824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{100} = 81\\cdot 3^{96}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, this translates to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f4712877225f8921bb6e4e046288c779087fe2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3^{96} &gt; 4\\cdot 2^{100} = 64\\cdot 2^{96}.\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"15\" />\nWe now prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711c704e4b05850f64dcfb01973f4c2c1e6a398b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3/2)^k &gt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\nClearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bb275c50c8814c54360c56885136ec241ac91c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3/2)^2 = 2.25 &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"138\" height=\"19\" />. Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711c704e4b05850f64dcfb01973f4c2c1e6a398b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3/2)^k &gt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/e/19e4194d33d81c3dd5ac49c773335504c4a7a0d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daa2496ef39b846dffe9ec7c99e8c72b8960d445.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^{k+1} &gt; \\frac{3k}{2} = k + \\frac{k}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"180\" height=\"47\" />. But since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/b/f9b030e449e5d47a4a6ded2bf6c5b3ce570734ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k/2 \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/0/e40e7aca3dce58c4169291163105477d6b392e2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3/2)^{k+1} &gt; k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />. By induction (and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is trivial), the claim is proven.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/4/304df158aa840a959d0b5b2b813cdcadeda3f20c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^{96} &gt; 96 &gt; 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"138\" height=\"46\" />. Writing this proof backwards and dividing both sides of the initial equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/e/66eb2b266d9ba8db4a637a2d9f579fef68926243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80 &lt; \\frac{3^{100}+2^{100}}{3^{96}+2^{96}} &lt; 81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"169\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_11\">Solution 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that in this problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/47035c5ad4780087b6537f0ad95588ef1358dc37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{96}+2^{96}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" /> times some number is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f21754fb78c76f7f280144bd8fc4165dabbddbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{100}+2^{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" />. Multiplying answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" /> or 81 to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/47035c5ad4780087b6537f0ad95588ef1358dc37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{96}+2^{96}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/cefb1e1620db03503fefff0dcd49a7fdd31561ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{100}+2^{96}\\cdot3^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/8/e388643ce290e03a1329959f8180f0fec20f2ce0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^4\\cdot2^{96}$\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/6/4a62d9023875220ea7eb3a22159656b4986e1808.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{100}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, so that means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" /> or 81 is too big. That leaves us with only one solution: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/c/07c6502089aa63f38907211076f7d1c8e9012216.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 80}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"111\" height=\"28\" /> \n</p><p>~ Terribleteeth\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_12\">Solution 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b762d6464d39cdf0f6ecfd3625957fba6acf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{96}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> in both numerator and denominator, this fraction can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/d/d1dafddfabd6e6cecd61eb350d8720475b7abcca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{81 \\times (1.5)^{96} + 16}{(1.5)^{96} + 1}.\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"44\" /> Notice that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/7/1178af8fcc5f3f3acb9f151f7dcc2c4eefe88fd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0dfca071d85ad280745111de75d6b0dbfb50db07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> will be so insignificant compared to a number such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/3/85350e1fcbb6f3b7e641d97b3c82c5a419b764bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1.5)^{96},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"21\" /> and that thereby the fraction will be ever so slightly less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />. Thereby, we see that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1de936550deb5ca3935da310c7edf5855a1f1a95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(A)} \\ 80}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~ Professor-Mom [&amp; wow there are now 12 sols to this problem :o :o :o this problem xDD]\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_13_.28slightly_similar_to_Solution_7.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_13_(slightly_similar_to_Solution_7)\">Solution 13 (slightly similar to Solution 7)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 13 (slightly similar to Solution 7)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce29fbb5ccd59f4042f6f3dc3677e155621118e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3^{96} + 2^{96})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"21\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/a/d5a2e615b8a5761b2d15f8c9aea61b084b8f4533.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3^{4} + 2^{4})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"21\" /> (to get the exponent up to 100), you'll get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/f/09f1eb7bbf8435ecc2371c34745b4091bb5f6b13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3^{100} + 2^{100}) + 3^{96} \\cdot 2^{4} + 2^{96} \\cdot 3^{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"248\" height=\"21\" />. Thus, in the numerator, if you add and subtract by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5630201c6f6133e2cdc88753432828e7a442a8b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{96} \\cdot 2^{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/d/8cd3372ca016c5d05a082c2f24b4586aed857d45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{96} \\cdot 3^{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" />, you'll get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddc7f704a6f60002a38308ea594e351316ff151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(3^{4} + 2^{4})(3^{100} + 2^{100}) - 3^{96} \\cdot 2^{4} - 2^{96} \\cdot 3^{4}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"321\" height=\"42\" />. You can then take out out the first number to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/d/bbd5275ab73715cbeb7e7fe1e18ce137185661a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{4} + 2^{4} - \\frac{3^{96} \\cdot 2^{4} + 2^{96} \\cdot 3^{4}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"211\" height=\"42\" />. This can then be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/a/99a915433cb81438f60ca62e16e7f0c43f3c168b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$87 - \\frac{16 \\cdot 3^{96} + 16 \\cdot 2^{96} + 75 \\cdot 2^{96}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"254\" height=\"42\" />, factoring out the 16 and splitting the fraction will give you <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cfa948b60c0348259178ec85f29f29cbc69c182.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$87 - 16 - \\frac{65 \\cdot 2^{96}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"155\" height=\"42\" />, giving you <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e7a3fcc447c64d800a796da4fb6ab95c6ed6bdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81 - \\frac{65 \\cdot 2^{96}}{3^{96}+2^{96}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"115\" height=\"42\" />. While you can roughly say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/4/344dcf4533cc4b56e4110f4655ed2a49bec8b510.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{65 \\cdot 2^{96}}{3^{96}+2^{96}} &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"108\" height=\"42\" /> you can also notice that the only answer choice less than 81 is 80, thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1de936550deb5ca3935da310c7edf5855a1f1a95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(A)} \\ 80}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" /> \n</p><p>~ Zeeshan12 [Now there's 13&#160;:) ]\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_14_.28Factoring.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_14_(Factoring)\">Solution 14 (Factoring)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 14 (Factoring)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you factor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/b/01b8b3b79da786c67116bc975bbdae7a4c5e6e80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{100}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> from the numerator and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c4ffbe31bf0e1c069d077f6dfc86fd15d20d388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{96}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> from the denominator, you will get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/1144b67d4ae673a710aec5e7450b8309f10f2990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3^{100}\\left(1+(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{100})}{3^{96}\\left(1+(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{96})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -24px\" width=\"132\" height=\"57\" />. Divide the numerator and denominator by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c4ffbe31bf0e1c069d077f6dfc86fd15d20d388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{96}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/731f4009261e364e75ec8a8b9d65115151e031ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{81\\left(1+(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{100})}{\\left(1+(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{96})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -24px\" width=\"120\" height=\"57\" />. We see that every time we multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> by itself, it slightly decreases, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd7c39f6caf58223012a83492ea77ac36f565028.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+(\\frac{2}{3})^{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" /> will be ever so slightly smaller than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/b/68b8c961a30df18805bfb112d027152e7bf6b492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+(\\frac{2}{3})^{96}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, the decimal representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d355642f0cd535f6e1908d0b85a2b0183303138c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\left(1+(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{100})}{\\left(1+(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{96})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -24px\" width=\"99\" height=\"57\" /> will be extremely close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so our solution will be the largest integer that is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1de936550deb5ca3935da310c7edf5855a1f1a95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(A)} \\ 80}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" /> \n</p><p>~andy_lee\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zb0AcwIDqdg\">https://youtu.be/zb0AcwIDqdg</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A\">2018 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a 